#%PAM-1.0
# ============================================================
#  NYXUS — PAM stack for the greetd login (installed to /etc/pam.d/greetd)
#  © 2026 JOSEPH A. SIERENGOWSKI · NYX-J5W-2026-SIERENGOWSKI-LOCKED
#
#  Password-only. This deliberately does NOT include system-local-login,
#  which carries `auth sufficient pam_fprintd.so`. With fprintd in the stack
#  the greetd IPC auth conversation emits a "Place your finger on the reader"
#  PAM prompt, and regreet renders it as a wide bar across the bottom of the
#  login screen (the "place your fingerprint" design flaw). Using system-login
#  (which has no fprintd) gives a clean themed password card with no stray bar.
#
#  Fingerprint auth is untouched everywhere else — sudo and TTY `login` keep
#  their own pam_fprintd entries (see /etc/pam.d/sudo, system-local-login).
# ============================================================
auth       include    system-login
account    include    system-login
password   include    system-login
session    include    system-login
